{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T01:11:46.208Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0253287c7b07e97397888a5e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-05T01:11:46.208Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Fixture timing isolated repeated npm registry/cache checks as a major local bottleneck: the same existing numeric-pagination workflow case passed in 299.94 seconds normally and 67.47 seconds total with NPM_CONFIG_PREFER_OFFLINE=true and the public npm configuration. Interrupted the first full npm run with exit 130 after verifying and stopping only its own process group; it is not counted as passing. Restarted the entire suite with cache preference, NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null, isolated Git config, low priority and at most two workers. Versions, fixtures, assertions, coverage scope and thresholds are unchanged; missing packages still use the registry. The focused suite remains 69 passed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T01:11:46.208Z"}],"before_hash":"b427e901bedb86b6467e3651f2c23762a33c69b17d8464a79d13aff816327f51","after_hash":"0d7d9baaca6bc1198f72529a63cfdbe72362020938e99f4e9d4894f3ee277204","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3d5e385aa5217ab7cdf38fb9faa9926a50330c0c7aa20409def9061d0b4f34ee"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T01:19:54.728Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0253287c7b07e97397888a5e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/9","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-05T01:19:54.725Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"CI on aaffdb6 found one related integration failure: the publication-attestation scanner treated TypeScript template literals in the quoted workflow heredoc as unresolved shell execution. The run reported 1712 tests, 1711 passes and 1 failure, with all four source coverage percentages at 100; this is not a passing gate. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41943832975/job/126970983903 . Replaced only the generated launcher template literals with string concatenation. The attestation gate now passes, and the combined production-policy plus attestation suite passes 77 tests. No scanner policy, thresholds or merge decisions were changed. Full local npm tests continue using the public npm configuration and cache preference."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T01:19:54.728Z"}],"before_hash":"0d7d9baaca6bc1198f72529a63cfdbe72362020938e99f4e9d4894f3ee277204","after_hash":"e569f052d1419eb9499af7fd1f746827a5361bbda6cf45ef8f912fd168923b3b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4d965fb4e88a6a07a9443baebcef9c1e598a3eea09954a4a842140c9a6286540"