{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T01:43:50.321Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0253287c7b07e97397888a5e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/11","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-05T01:43:50.312Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Review found and fixed a custom-token event loop in the caller: auto_merge_enabled events can belong to the automation credential owner, so subscribing to them would immediately revoke a valid bot-only request under the required actor guard. Removed that event from the own caller and README snippet; synchronize remains subscribed. Added a two-event regression that executes the production policy: token-generated arm events preserve the request, then a foreign synchronize revokes it. Reintroducing only the old event subscription in a disposable copy makes that one behavioral test fail; the unchanged package worktree passes all 70 policy/workflow tests. Combined policy and publication-attestation tests pass 78 cases. Test typecheck, lint and publication-attestation gate pass. No predicate, permissions, thresholds or branch configuration changed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T01:43:50.321Z"}],"before_hash":"e02f4ed527c108f9894604643ae7752b31161772fa4128c11e085d134f31c684","after_hash":"c71c69a4bfd0871b273ae5c8a322132023007f1861606a61ca0add426aa4998c","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1259521b6c66803a0cd430c3a5e13eef57a6576f390e1ea51f1058250c368963"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T02:05:48.108Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0253287c7b07e97397888a5e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/12","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-05T02:05:48.106Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Native Bun found two default-adapter fixture failures: Bun command lookup used its startup environment when child_process options omitted env. A unique local-command probe reproduced the difference without network access: implicit lookup failed under Bun while an explicit environment resolved the fixture on Node and Bun. The earlier dynamic-PATH default-gh probe escaped its intended stub and was rejected against the synthetic target; no arm or squash operation was requested. The adapter now snapshots the current environment explicitly, and default-adapter coverage runs in child processes with fixture PATH present at startup. Added a unique-command regression; reverting only the environment option makes that one Bun test fail without any real gh fallback. Fixed source passes 71 native Bun tests and 79 combined Node policy/attestation tests. Pinned pm linked test execution also passes. Test typecheck, lint and docstrings pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T02:05:48.108Z"}],"before_hash":"c71c69a4bfd0871b273ae5c8a322132023007f1861606a61ca0add426aa4998c","after_hash":"e75e523a2e4499b20278e660660726ba15a6746132b68224c4a695d2f65d69ef","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9b25bf35b883228285a56460565864239bd193d45607452f024e308b562ba991"}
